# ThreadSanitizer suppressions, used by the linux-tsan test preset (Architecture.md: Memory and threads).
# Only races inside third-party code, each with the library and the reason.

# SQLite, WAL mode with several connections (library/: search on the frontend's thread, scan on the library thread).
# The wal-index header in shared memory is read without a lock by design: readers copy it twice and compare the
# copies plus a checksum, and retry on a mismatch (sqlite3.c, walIndexTryHdr and the comments around it). TSan sees
# the unlocked memcpy against the writer's update.
race:walIndexWriteHdr
race:walIndexTryHdr
race:walTryBeginRead

# libdbus, used by SDL (screensaver and portal handling) in SDL_Init and SDL_Quit. The app tests (player-ui) start and
# stop SDL several times in one process; dbus takes its connection lock and the global lock in different orders in
# dbus_connection_close and the first use of a new connection. Inside the system library, not in djw code.
deadlock:libdbus-1.so
